             University of Houston -- Information Technology

               Computer Usage Policy / Network Access Form


   The University of Houston's computing facilities service a large number of
faculty and students.  All users have the responsibility to use the Univeristy
computing systems in an effective, efficient, ethical, and lawful manner.  The
ethical and legal standards that are to be maintained are derived directly from
standards of common sense and common decency that apply to the use of any 
public resource.

   The following is a policy summary.  A copy of the complete policy statement
is available in publication cabinets and is posted at Information Technology
sites.

As a condition of use of any of the computing facilities, the user agrees to
respect:

	* the privacy of other users' files, tapes, and passwords,

	* the legal protection (copyright) of software and data,

	* the intended usage for which access was granted,

	* the integrity of computing systems,

	* the financial structure (or charges) of a computing system,

	* the shared nature of the computing resources, and

	* the rights of other users.

   Violations of these conditions are certainly unethical and may be violations
of University policy of criminal offenses.  Users are expected to report to the
facility manager, or to the individual in charge of their computing resource,
information they may have concerning instances in which the above conditions
have been or are being violated.

I agree to use the UH systems in accordance with the UH computer usage policy.

